 "changes": [
  "REMOVED Castellón de la Plana. It was a low-confidence filler city, and no search found it as an ETS2 city. The wiki.gg Vila-real page shows the game's city on the AP-7 in that area is Vila-real. A ProMods forum post says vanilla lacks Castellón.",
  "REMOVED Logroño. No city page or depot was found. The wiki.gg A-1 (Spain) page mentions it only as a route waypoint (Burgos-Logroño segment). Its 5 edges are replaced by Bilbao-Zaragoza 305 km, Burgos-Zaragoza 290 km and Burgos-Pamplona 210 km (via Vitoria). The low-confidence Logroño-Soria N-111 edge is dropped.",
  "ADDED Vila-real (ES, Iberia, 39.938/-0.101, aliases Villarreal). wiki.gg: 'Vila-real (Spanish: Villarreal) is a city in Spain that is featured in the Iberia map expansion', with a Domdepo depot and a garage.",
  "ADDED Port de Sagunt (ES, Iberia, 39.660/-0.228, aliases Puerto de Sagunto/Sagunto). wiki.gg: town featured in the Iberia DLC, with ACC and CGLA factories and a TDC Auto Terminal depot. The wiki's Spain list of 39 cities includes it, between València and Vila-real.",
  "ADDED Vandellòs (ES, Iberia, coordinates of the Vandellòs II plant 40.951/0.866), conf medium. wiki.gg: 'In-game, Vandellòs consists only of the Vandellòs II Nuclear Power Plant', with an Iberatómica depot (same pattern as Almaraz). The Japanese wiki (wikiwiki.jp ets2steam Iberia) lists it, but one search summary said the wiki.gg Spain city list omits it.",
  "ROADS: split the coastal AP-7 Valencia-Tarragona corridor (formerly via Castellón) into Valencia-Port de Sagunt 30, Port de Sagunt-Vila-real 45, Vila-real-Vandellòs 145 and Vandellòs-Tarragona 40, about 260 km in total, as before.",
  "ROADS: replaced Valencia-Teruel (145) with Port de Sagunt-Teruel (118, A-23), because the A-23 joins the coast at Sagunt. Valencia-Teruel is now 148 km.",
  "Mérida: kept, conf high->medium, with a note. The wiki.gg Mérida page calls it 'an inaccessible city' and the map-data project lists it as a village, so it probably has no depots. It still appears to count toward the wiki's 39 Spanish cities (51 Iberia cities in total), and it is the A-5/A-66 junction, so it was not disproved as an in-game city entry.",
  "CITY COUNT: the previous file had 38 ES + 12 PT = 50, not 51 as stated. It now has 39 ES + 12 PT = 51, which matches wiki.gg's 'Iberia: 51 cities (49 at release + Beja and Soria in 1.43)' and '39 cities in Spain'.",
  "PORTUGAL: all 12 confirmed by the fandom wiki's Portugal city list: Beja, Coimbra, Cortiçadas de Lavre, Évora, Faro, Guarda, Lisboa, Olhão, Ponte de Sor, Porto, Setúbal, Sines. Cortiçadas de Lavre raised from medium to high.",
  "NOT ADDED (radio_only candidates): Huesca, Irun, La Jonquera, Manresa, Mengíbar, San Sebastián/Donostia. None appears in any vanilla Iberia city evidence, and they fit the ProMods Iberia additions. The 39-city Spanish count is already filled.",
  "FERRIES: none added. No vanilla ferry from an Iberian port was found, and Santander-Plymouth is not vanilla (Plymouth is not in the base-game UK). The graph was checked: all 51 cities are connected, and the cross-border edges to Perpignan and Bayonne (FR) are kept."
 ],
 "sources": "WebSearch (14 calls), working only from result text. trucksimulator.wiki.gg pages: Iberia, Euro_Truck_Simulator_2:_Iberia (51 cities: 49 at release + 2 in 1.43), Spain ('39 cities in Spain'), Vila-real, Port_de_Sagunt, Vandellòs, Mérida ('an inaccessible city'), Soria, A-1_(Spain) (Logroño only as a waypoint), Scenery_towns/Euro_Truck_Simulator_2/Spain. truck-simulator.fandom.com Portugal navbox via A7/A12/A28 (Portugal) pages (12 PT cities). wikiwiki.jp/ets2steam/DLC/Iberia (lists Vandellòs). promods.net viewtopic.php?p=217775 (Castellón not in vanilla; ProMods used Vinaròs). blog.scssoft.com Iberia posts (2020-2021)."
}